## Caveat — bare `Hair_00_HAIR`

Single-material hairstyles export as `N00_000_Hair_00_HAIR (Instance)` with no `_{NN}` layer suffix. It belongs to the strand **`Hair` object**, not the `Body` back-of-head slot.

`clean_vroid_material_names.py` currently maps this case to **`Hair.Back`** (rule "primary / non-stranded hair"). That name is misleading: `Hair.Back` is the [tri-to-quad-uv-map](../../skills/tri-to-quad-uv-map/SKILL.md) `hairback` profile token, whose CSV assumes the fixed **body** UV atlas — replaying it on a strand mesh would dissolve against the wrong atlas.

Agent action after Phase B on a single-material hairstyle: rename `Hair.Back` → **`Hair.01`**, and patch matching values in `scene["vroid_material_rename_map"]`. Do this **before Phase C** so texture slugs come out `hair_01_base` / `hair_01_normal` rather than `hair_back_*`.

Reserve `Hair.Back` for a material actually assigned to a `Body` slot.

## Lookup

Use `resolve_material_by_token("Face.Skin")` from `clean_vroid_material_names.py` — accepts workflow token, VRoid tail, or full import name.

Texture slugs: dots → underscores (`Face.Skin` → `face_skin`).
